        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{\\$3}{\\text{kg}}$",
          "worked": "Option 1:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\$1.80}{200\\text{ g}}&=\\frac{\\$1.80\\times5}{200\\text{ g}\\times5}=\\frac{\\$9}{1\\text{ kg}}\n\\end{align*}$$\nOption 2:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\$9}{750\\text{ g}}&=\\frac{\\$9\\div3}{750\\text{ g}\\div3}=\\frac{\\$3}{250\\text{ g}}\\\\\n\\frac{\\$9}{750\\text{ g}}&=\\frac{\\$3\\times4}{250\\text{ g}\\times4}=\\frac{\\$12}{1\\text{ kg}}\\\\\n\\text{Difference per kg}&=\\$12-\\$9=\\$3\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe difference is $\\frac{\\$3}{\\text{kg}}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
